{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for",
    "sg13cmos5l-startup-trip-point (issue #337, Part of #322). Same grid and",
    "measurements as the legacy run_pvt_sweep.sh loop; instantiated by",
    "run_klt_sim.sh via sim/harness/cmos5l_klt.py, which substitutes @@BODY@@",
    "and @@CORNER_BUNDLE@@ (local sanity) or splits per process x supply",
    "(batch).",
    "",
    "WHY PER-SUPPLY. The dc sweep's stop value and two measurement levels",
    "scale with the supply: the legacy loop sweeps Vsns1 0..VDD (step 5 mV),",
    "measures the trip point at v(det) = VDD/2 and the 'core fully up' end",
    "state one step short of VDD (ngspice refuses `.meas at=` at the exact",
    "end of a dc sweep). cmos5l_klt.py substitutes @@VDD@@, @@VDD_HALF@@",
    "(%.4f of VDD/2) and @@VDD_OFF@@ (%.4f of VDD-0.05), as the legacy",
    "script's awk did, and runs one request per supply with",
    "`corners.supply_v` pinned to that supply.",
    "",
    "The legacy `op` before the sweep (cold-start state, sns1 = 0) is the",
    "first point of the dc sweep: det_on_v / fb_on_v are measured `at=0`,",
    "the sweep start. Whether ngspice's `.meas dc ... at=` accepts the exact",
    "start point has NOT been verified here (no simulation was run for",
    "issue #337); the run_klt_sim.sh --sanity gate exercises it on one local",
    "corner before any grid is dispatched.",
    "",
    "The pass/fail verdict (six criteria) is NOT expressible as a `limits`",
    "block against one measurement; sim/harness/cmos5l_klt.py enrich",
    "--kind trip-point re-grades each point with the legacy formula."
  ],
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "netlist": "@@BODY@@",
  "netlist_source": "extracted",
  "models": { "lib": "@@CORNER_BUNDLE@@" },
  "corners": {
    "process": ["typ", "bcs", "wcs", "sf", "fs"],
    "supply_v": { "Vvdd": [2.97, 3.3, 3.63] },
    "temperature_c": [-40, 27, 125]
  },
  "analysis": { "kind": "dc", "args": "Vsns1 0 @@VDD@@ 0.005" },
  "measurements": [
    { "name": "det_on_v", "spice": ".meas dc det_on_v find v(det) at=0" },
    { "name": "fb_on_v", "spice": ".meas dc fb_on_v find v(fb) at=0" },
    { "name": "vtrip_v", "spice": ".meas dc vtrip_v when v(det)=@@VDD_HALF@@ cross=1" },
    { "name": "det_off_v", "spice": ".meas dc det_off_v find v(det) at=@@VDD_OFF@@" },
    { "name": "fb_off_v", "spice": ".meas dc fb_off_v find v(fb) at=@@VDD_OFF@@" }
  ],
  "options": {
    "timeout_s": 300,
    "keep_artifacts": true
  }
}
